## Tasks (`mise.toml`)

Git hooks and CI call the same `mise` tasks (Python <python_major_minor>+ via `uv`):

- `mise run install`: `uv sync --locked` (malware-checked) + git hooks.
- `mise run format`: `ruff` (imports + format) and `dprint`.
- `mise run check`: `check:local` (`jactionlint`, `ruff`, `ty`, `deptry`, `dprint`, `betterleaks`, `lychee`, `typos`, `validate-pyproject`, `uv lock --check`, `check:tasks` via `mise tasks validate` and `lefthook validate`) + `check:network` (`uv audit`).
- `mise run test`: offline `pytest` (`pytest-socket` loopback-only, 60s timeout, 85% branch coverage).
- `mise run build`: `uv build --clear --no-sources` (add `build:docs` / `test:integration` / `test:e2e` tasks when opted in).
- **Fast inner loop**: `uv run --locked pytest -q <path>::<test>`, `uv run --locked pytest -q -x -l --lf`, `uv run --locked ruff check <path>`, `uv run --locked ty check <path>`; finish with full `mise` gates.

## Conventions

- Done requires clean `mise run format`, `check`, `test`, and `build` locally (plus opted-in `build:docs`, `test:integration`, and `test:e2e`), normal/boundary/failure tests for changed behavior, synced docs, and clean-context reviewer `supagents` checks on non-trivial changes.
- Declare only used dependencies (`deptry` enforces), use modern Python annotations (`list[str]`, `X | Y`, `Annotated`), and add repo-specific boundaries here without repeating `~/.agents/AGENTS.md`.

## Layout

- `src/<package>/`: package exports (`__init__.py`, `__version__`) and cohesive domain modules.
- `tests/`: deterministic offline tests (`@pytest.mark.integration` opt-in only when needed).
- `.agents/skills/`, `.agents/supagents/`: project skills and static read-only reviewers (when used; content producers remain dynamic).
- `pyproject.toml`, `mise.toml`, `lefthook.yml`, `dprint.json`, `cliff.toml`: single sources of truth for config and pins.
